	(text "quantification of voltage noise:\n(5 / 10 / 20 kHz, peak-peak)\nDAC: 54 / 70 / 94 μV\nop amp input: 212 / 300 / 425 μV\n\nmodeling all relevant variables\n(mechanical Q = 100, G_master = 50)\nR_n = 50k, C_n = 0.255 nF: 4.9 / 9.4 / 16.7 pm\nR_n = 50k, C_n = 0.127 nF: 3.8 / 6.8 / 13.2 pm\nR_n = 50k, C_n = 0.076 nF: 3.3 / 5.5 / 10.3 pm\nR_n = 50k, C_n = 0.051 nF: 3.1 / 4.8 / 8.5 pm\n\nall of this optimization effort is defeated by the\nmaster's 50x gain amplifying its 400 μV input stage noise\n10.8 / 15.2 / 21.5 pm\n\nsolution: add OPA828 stage to reduce the needed gain factor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 99.568 14.478 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0a06cfde-34c1-44f2-97c9-f881258d7e2f")
	)
	(text "what elements to add to stabilize the slave, with -1 gain?\n\nresistor:\n40k (application note formula)\n20-60k (C_f = 0.01 pF)\n20-60k (C_f = 0.05 pF)\n30-90k (C_f = 0.1 pF)\n45-110k (C_f = 0.2 pF)\n\ncapacitor (50k, C_f = 0.05 pF)\n0.07 nF (simulation)\n\ncapacitor (50k, C_f = 0.2 pF)\n0.05 nF (simulation)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.352 19.558 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "104c26a8-3d35-42d7-835f-c653d6605118")
	)
	(text "impact of C_c, C_f on slew rate into piezo:\nTODO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 233.172 70.866 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1604a39f-ced7-4283-9036-9c2587a470de")
	)
	(text "Rf: 1206 or 1210 resistor\nkeepout zone on closest inner copper layer\nto make capacitance closer to expectation"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 21.336 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1e9263e1-d358-4384-aafe-ebe7d1cce42e")
	)
	(text "effect of gain on stability\n\n[C_f = 0.2 pF, C_c = 2.2 pF]\nno capacitive load: overshoot vanishes at G > 12.5\n- no R_n and C_n needed on master\n- 50k and 0.01-0.07n on slave\n- 40k and 0.02-0.10n on slave\n- 30k and 0.03-0.15n on slave\n- 20k and 0.04-0.20n on slave\nwith piezo:\n\n[C_f = 0.5 pF, C_c = 2.2 pF]\nno capacitive load: overshoot vanishes at G > 4.0\n- 70k and 3-30p\n- 50k and 7-40p\n- 20k and 30-150p\n\n[C_f = 0.2 pF, C_c = 10 pF]\nno capacitive load: overshoot vanishes at G > 5.7\n- 100k and 0.01-0.06n\n- 50k and 0.03-0.13n\n\n[C_f = 0.5 pF, C_c = 10 pF]\nno capacitive load: overshoot vanishes at G > 4.4\n- 130k and 5-30p\n- 70k and 9-60p\nwith piezo: overshoot never vanishes\n- G_m = 10, G_s = 8, C_n = 0.08n\n- G_m = 16, G_s = 8, C_n = ???\nnone of these are oscillations, just messy settling in <10 μs"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.606 70.104 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7d1cdc54-9514-4a4a-8a7e-1bda86ec8858")
	)
	(text "current limit\n\nsafe vs. design requirement\nmaster: 15 Ω / 6 Ω\nslave: 12 Ω / 5 Ω\n\nthe safe limits are to help in a\nfault condition where the current shorts\n\nit will be easier to test with the safe ones\nfirst, and once we have experience,\nreplace with more optimized resistors\n\ndesign the board to make broken amplifiers\neasily replaced\n\nonly do this modification on the amplifier for\nthe Z axis, or whichever one resists gravity"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 238.76 20.828 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ccac41a3-dbeb-43e0-81d9-eca7462d994b")
	)
